<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Silves</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shilb</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Silves is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arade">Arade</a> river in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a>, southern Portugal. As Shilb it was the chief city of the Islamic Algarve, known for its poets and its red sandstone castle, and the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifas</a> of the Banu Muzayn and later Ibn al-Mundhir. Sancho I of Portugal took it with crusader help in 1189, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> recovered it in 1191, and Portugal conquered it finally in the 1240s.</p></div>
